@/* 
** ++
**
**  Facility:  DSP - DSP code
**
**  Abstract:
**      DSP code to implement the ripple loop
**
**  Author:
**      R. Claus & P. Corredoura, SLAC/PEP-II Low Level RF Project
**
**  History:
** 3:33pm July  10, 2006 - W. Ross -- name: s3phs4ripple.s
**                         Cut number of fast coefficients down from
**                         34 to 26 to accomodate higher sampling
**                         frequency of Spear 3.
** 8:33am Mar   30, 2006 - W. Ross -- name: phs4ripple.s
**                         Modified to remove some non-understandable
**                         'saturation' code. Changed so that most
**                         linear operations are now performed with
**                         accumulators set for saturation on output.
**                         Saturation is suppressed for offset binary
**                         to/from 2s Complement conversions only.
**10:13am Mar   15, 2006 - W. Ross -- new name: phs4ripple.s
**                         Amplitude Estimator code is removed to obtain
**                         cycle time to perform Phase Estimation using
**                         double precision multiplication.  Initially,
**                         34 fast phase harmonics and 4 slow phase
**                         harmonics are implimented.
**        Feb    1, 2006 - W. Ross
**                         Code is modified to utilize the Klystron
**                         ADC now available in the Rev 4 RFP Module
**                         in place of Klystron data received from the
**                         IQ&A module.  In doing this, the software
**                         FIFO for the reference signal is no longer
**                         required and is removed from the code. Also
**                         removed timing comments, no longer accurate.
**        Jan   13, 1998 - Robert C. Sass
**                         Because I/QKlys are delayed ~1msec but I/Qref
**                         are delayed only ~44usec., pipeline I/Qref so
**                         ref and klys are ~from the same time.
**        Nov   19, 1997 - Robert C. Sass
**                         Many changes and cleanup.
**        Nov    6, 1997 - Robert C. Sass
**                         Use AmpSet for open loop.
**        Oct    3, 1997 - Add new downloads. R. Sass
**        Sept  23, 1997 - Change calc of Phase error to:
**                         PhsErr = PhsRef - PhsKly
**        April 18, 1997 - Interlaced reading Qref, Qkly, Ikly,Iref
**        April 17, 1997 - New version started.  Further attempts at
**                         optimization so that we can add more harmonics.
**        October 20, 1996 - Created
**
**         Add slow harmonics, only one of which is processed each cycle. 
**         For the harmonics near 60 Hz, the coefficients are very close 
**         to 2.0 and the 16 bit word resolution so they don't work very 
**         well even at 12 KHz. We want to run at 23 KHz so we can cancel 
**         higher harmonics where they REALLY don't work well. By Adding 8 
**         slow harmonics, we have an effective sampling rate of ~3 KHz and 
**         so have reasonable coefficients to cancel harmonics up to ~1.5 KHz.
**
**         Nov 23, 1997 - Robert C. Sass
**                        Fix a few slow harmonic bugs. The last bug!!
**
